    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2QwaDKdXakBcmcPe1c8yRuN)_\n\n## What\nSome litnote `pub-title` lines enclose the title in quotes. `sp-litnotes-meta` now detects and fixes them.\n\n- `sp-litnotes-meta--unquote` strips quotes (straight and curly) only when they wrap the whole value; inner quotes stay (`\"A\" and \"B\"` is left alone).\n- Batch fill (`-fill-all-dryrun` / `-convert`): a quoted title is its own category (\"Quoted pub-title\", counted and listed with old -> new). Convert removes the quotes with the existing backup, batch of 50, pick/choose and drop-and-stash handling. `sp-litnotes-meta-fill` (single note) does it too.\n- The BibTeX title is read without enclosing quotes (`{\"Title\"}`), so the changed-field update from #361 cannot reintroduce them.\n- New `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-title-lint-dryrun` / `-convert` (on `sp-batch-report`, like the bib-parent lint) also reach notes with no citation key or no .bib entry.\n- Literate doc updated (bullet-pointed); no CHANGELOG edits.\n\n## Testing\n`tests/sp-litnotes-meta-test.el`: 54 tests pass on Emacs 29 (new ones cover unquoting, BibTeX titles, the dry-run category, convert, update-changed and the lint). Not run on the real vault.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAsmZG5tiGhctahjhB)_",
